.TH SCAN_OCTAL 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
scan_octal \- Scan an octal number from a string

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/scan.h>

.IB size_t
.IB scan_octal(const char* src, uint64* dest);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBscan_octal\fR function scans an octal number from a given string and stores the result in a provided destination.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IB src
The input string containing the octal number.
.TP
.IB dest
The destination where the scanned octal number will be stored.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns the number of characters processed.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBscan_octal\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/scan.h>

int main() {
    const char* octal = "1234";
    uint64 dest;
    size_t length = scan_octal(octal, &dest);
    printf("Scanned octal: %llu\n", dest);
    printf("Length processed: %zu\n", length);
    return 0;
}
.nef